          "blocks": {
            "accordion_row_GEiwcK": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "How do you clean a leather bag?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_adbV9w": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>To clean a leather bag, gently remove dust using a soft, dry cloth. For light cleaning, use a slightly damp cloth and wipe the surface carefully without saturating the leather. Allow it to air dry naturally. Avoid harsh chemicals or unsuitable cleaning products, as they may damage fine leather. For delicate or valuable pieces, professional leather care is recommended.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_adbV9w"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_Gi3k7Y": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Can leather get wet?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_4UkVhD": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Leather can tolerate small amounts of moisture, but excessive exposure to water may cause stains, stiffness, or changes in color. If your leather bag becomes wet, gently pat it dry with a soft cloth and allow it to dry at room temperature. Avoid direct heat, which can damage the material.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_4UkVhD"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_KEHFCx": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "How often should you condition leather?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_CqznBN": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>High-quality full-grain leather requires minimal conditioning. Depending on use, applying a suitable conditioner every few months helps maintain softness and prevent drying. Over-conditioning should be avoided, as it may alter the natural character and patina of the leather.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_CqznBN"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_g4e3jW": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "What is full-grain leather?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_WWFqPe": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Full-grain leather is the highest quality leather available, taken from the outermost layer of the hide where the fibers are the most dense and durable. This layer, often referred to as the “grain,” remains completely intact and unaltered, preserving the leather’s natural surface.</p><p>Because the grain is not sanded or corrected, full-grain leather retains its original characteristics - including pores, veins, and subtle variations in texture. These natural features are a sign of authenticity and contribute to the strength and longevity of the material.</p><p>Beneath the grain lies a tightly structured network of fibers, which gives full-grain leather its exceptional resistance to wear while allowing it to remain breathable. Over time, this structure enables the leather to soften and develop a rich patina.</p><p>In contrast, top-grain leather is lightly sanded to remove surface irregularities and often finished with coatings to create a more uniform appearance. While still high quality, this process reduces the natural strength and prevents the leather from aging in the same way as full-grain leather.</p><p>Lower layers of the hide are used for genuine leather, which is typically processed and coated. These materials lack the durability, breathability, and character of full-grain leather.</p><p>For this reason, full-grain leather is used in luxury leather goods and handmade leather bags, where material integrity, longevity, and natural beauty are essential.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_WWFqPe"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_Ab7q7c": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Why is full-grain leather considered the best?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_WWMcVz": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Full-grain leather preserves the strongest part of the hide, making it highly resistant and long-lasting. Unlike corrected leather, it ages naturally and develops character, which is why it is used in luxury leather goods and handmade leather products.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
