              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_UmGbzP": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "How do you maintain a leather bag?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_6RpXLx": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Maintaining a leather bag requires consistent, minimal care to preserve its structure, texture, and appearance over time. High-quality leather, especially full-grain leather, improves with proper handling rather than intensive treatment.</p><p>For daily and long-term <strong>leather maintenance</strong>, follow these principles:</p><ul><li>Gently wipe the surface with a soft, dry cloth to remove dust</li><li>Avoid prolonged exposure to sunlight, heat, or humidity</li><li>Handle with clean hands to prevent oils and stains</li><li>Keep away from water and harsh surfaces</li><li>Store the bag in a dust bag when not in use</li><li>Maintain its shape with soft filling</li><li>Condition occasionally using products suitable for fine leather</li></ul><p>Rather than frequent intervention, leather benefits from careful use and a stable environment. With the right care, it will develop a natural patina and retain its elegance for many years.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
